    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Every year the Founders Day Festival turns the town square into a tapestry of homemade pies, off‑key band music, and painted‑butterfly kids.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.wikixm.com/us/pa/hilldale/overview"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Miller’s Pond, the town’s unofficial centerpiece, reflects autumn leaves, winter ice, and spring fishermen’s hopeful chatter.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.wikixm.com/us/pa/hilldale/overview"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Hilldale Diner, with chrome accents and endless coffee, doubles as the town’s living room where football gossip meets council debate.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.wikixm.com/us/pa/hilldale/overview"
    },
    {
